   "nav": "FAQ",
   "items": [
    {
     "q": "Can we release water on online TOC and conductivity?",
     "a": "Yes, for total organic carbon (TOC) and conductivity, once qualification shows the online readings match point-of-use samples. USP <643> and <645> allow online tests. Microbial counts stay laboratory tests.",
     "link": "svc-cq"
    },
    {
     "q": "Our transmitters show compensated conductivity. Is that a problem?",
     "a": "For trending, no. USP <645> stage 1 compares the uncompensated reading with the table row at or below the measured temperature. Compensation can pass water stage 1 would fail. We store both."
    },
    {
     "q": "Which Part 11 clauses need our procedures?",
     "a": "No system is Part 11 compliant on its own: your site complies through its validated system and its procedures. Our Part 11 and Annex 11 assessment shows which clauses need a site procedure."
    },
    {
     "q": "Do we get full access to the PLC and HMI code?",
     "a": "[code delivered unlocked, and who owns it]. The code's version and checksum are recorded at the factory acceptance test (FAT) [confirm]. You can then show the running code is the tested code.",
     "link": "cmp-quality#buying",
     "link_label": "How buying from us works"
    },
